[94.366328, "o", "Done. `vectorops` is built and a local PyPI index is running on port 8080.\r\n\r\n**What was created in `/app`**\r\n- `vectorops/__init__.py` — `dotproduct(a, b)` (length-checked, `sum(x*y ...)`) plus `__version__ = \"0.1.0\"`\r\n- `pyproject.toml` — setuptools build, version `0.1.0`\r\n- `dist/` — `vectorops-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl` and `.tar.gz`\r\n- `packages/` — the artifacts served by pypiserver\r\n- `serve.sh` — rebuilds and serves the index (`PORT` env, default 8080)\r\n- `tests/test_dotproduct.py` — 6 pytest cases\r\n- `README.md`\r\n\r\n**Server**\r\n`pypi-server` is running on `0.0.0.0:8080` with `--disable-fallback` (local only, no proxy to pypi.org). `/simple/vectorops/` returns 200 listing both artifacts; an unknown package returns 404, confirming no upstream fallback.\r\n\r\n**Verification** (fresh venv, exact command from the spec):\r\n```\r\n$ pip install --no-cache-dir --index-url http://localhost:8080/simple vectorops==0.1.0\r\nLooking in indexes: http://localhost:8080/simple\r\nDownloading http://localhost:8080/packa"]
[94.366359, "o", "ges/vectorops-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl\r\nSuccessfully installed vectorops-0.1.0\r\n\r\n$ python -c \"from vectorops import dotproduct; assert 1 == dotproduct([1,1], [0,1])\"\r\ninstalled 0.1.0 from .../site-packages/vectorops/__init__.py\r\n```\r\n`pytest tests -q` → `6 passed`.\r\n\r\nNote: the server is a background process of this session. If it stops, restart with `/app/serve.sh` (rebuilds everything and serves on 8080).\r\n"]
